# Teysa Karlov makes Sphinx of False Conclusions' "When this creature dies, if it isn't a token, create a token that's a
# copy of it" trigger twice (CR 603.2d): each triggering checks its intervening "if" as it triggers and again as it
# resolves (CR 603.4) - the dead Sphinx, as it last existed, was no token - and each makes a token. The tokens are
# creature tokens Bot1 controls, so Teysa gives them vigilance and lifelink ("Creature tokens you control have vigilance
# and lifelink"); Teysa itself, no token, has neither. On turn 5 a token Sphinx dies: it was a token, so its ability does
# not trigger at all, doubled or not.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Teysa Karlov
Sphinx of False Conclusions
Lightning Bolt
Lightning Bolt
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains x14

